Package: zirbe
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: David M. Anderson <david.anderson@excelano.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: mail
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/excelano/zirbe-desktop
Depends: libc6, libgcc-s1, libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0, libjavascriptcoregtk-4.1-0, libgtk-3-0t64 | libgtk-3-0, libglib2.0-0t64 | libglib2.0-0, libcairo2, libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0, libsoup-3.0-0, libdbus-1-3, libwayland-client0, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libegl1, libvulkan1 | libgl1, libx11-6, libx11-xcb1, libxi6, libxcursor1, libxrandr2, libfontconfig1, libfreetype6, ca-certificates, desktop-file-utils, hicolor-icon-theme
Recommends: gnome-keyring
Description: Email that reads like a conversation
 Zirbe shows the mail in an IMAP account as conversations: a thread is one
 conversation, its subject is the name, the people on it are the members,
 and each message is a bubble. Replies go to everyone in the conversation
 and keep the thread together for every other mail program.
 .
 Passwords are kept in the desktop keyring and mail in a private cache.
 The only network connections are to the mail servers you sign in to.
